<title>UK: Caradon H1 pretax profit falls 8.9 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Caradon H1 pretax profit falls 8.9 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.2		    vs 8.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.9		    vs 2.9</p>
<p> Pretax		     81.3		   vs 90.2</p>
<p> Turnover		   1.06 billion	 vs 1.03 billion</p>
<p>NOTE - UK building products group Caradon Plc said market conditions continued to be difficult, but it was benefitting from the successful launch of new products since the start of 1996. This, along with cost cuts and investments in efficiencies, would provide momentum in 1997, Caradon said.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 84.7		   vs 92.6</p>
<p> Interest payable	 3.8		    vs 3.3</p>
<p> Tax charge		 30.6		   vs 32.4</p>
<p> Net taxed		  50.7		   vs 57.8</p>
<p> Retained profit	  26.0		   vs 32.6</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 22</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 1  Ex-div date		Sept 23</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7972</p>
</text>
